# CPLEX baseline parameters (FlexTool default).
#
# Format: one "<name> <value>" per line using the names of the CPLEX
# interactive optimizer's ``set`` command (e.g. ``threads``, ``timelimit``,
# ``mip tolerances mipgap``); "#" starts a comment.  Write the full names: a
# dotted name (mip.tolerances.mipgap) is read as the spaced one, but an
# abbreviation (mip tol mipg) is not matched with the full name.
#
# FlexTool turns each line into ``set <name> <value>`` and pipes it to the
# ``cplex`` interactive optimizer before ``read <mps>`` / ``optimize``
# (flextool/engine/solve/_subprocess_solve.py).  A .prm file is not used: its
# version header must match the installed CPLEX exactly.
#
# Precedence (later wins): this file < the solve's solver_mip_gap < the solve's
# solver_arguments < the run's --solver-mip-gap / --solver-time-limit (or
# FLEXTOOL_SOLVER_MIP_GAP / FLEXTOOL_SOLVER_TIME_LIMIT; the GUI's time limit).
# Names match without regard to case; one value per parameter is passed.
#
# FlexTool reads this file from the run's solver_config folder (see
# docs/solvers/index.md, "Where the option files come from") and copies it to
# <work folder>/solve_data/solver_config/ as the record of the run.
#
# Reference: https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/icos/22.1.0?topic=cplex-list-parameters
#
# Conservative defaults — edit to suit your model.
# Replaced by the run's --threads (Threads per run in the FlexTool window) when it is given.
threads 1
mip tolerances mipgap 0.002
